From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pigweed: cipd_setup/wrapper.py: support linux-riscv64

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted to google/pigweed]

cipd_setup/wrapper.py bootstraps the standalone `cipd` client binary
used by Pigweed's env setup. Two separate bugs there make it reject
riscv64 entirely, even though the CIPD backend itself already serves a
linux-riscv64 client (chrome-infra-packages.appspot.com, and
.cipd_version.digests lists a linux-riscv64 sha256 for the pinned
client version):

- arch_normalized() only special-cases arm/aarch64; everything else
  falls through to `machine.endswith('64')`, which maps the literal
  string "riscv64" to "amd64" because it also ends in "64".
- SUPPORTED_PLATFORMS is a hardcoded tuple that never listed
  "linux-riscv64" to begin with, so client_bytes() would raise
  UnsupportedPlatform even with the arch mapping fixed.

Neither function used by this wheel's actual package-selection logic
(cipd_setup/update.py:platform(), which already falls back to the
literal "riscv64" string) needs a patch; only the client bootstrap
path in this file does.

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 third_party/pigweed/repo/pw_env_setup/py/pw_env_setup/cipd_setup/wrapper.py | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/third_party/pigweed/repo/pw_env_setup/py/pw_env_setup/cipd_setup/wrapper.py b/third_party/pigweed/repo/pw_env_setup/py/pw_env_setup/cipd_setup/wrapper.py
index 151745d..75228bc 100644
--- a/third_party/pigweed/repo/pw_env_setup/py/pw_env_setup/cipd_setup/wrapper.py
+++ b/third_party/pigweed/repo/pw_env_setup/py/pw_env_setup/cipd_setup/wrapper.py
@@ -51,6 +51,7 @@ SUPPORTED_PLATFORMS = (
     'linux-mipsle',
     'linux-ppc64',
     'linux-ppc64le',
+    'linux-riscv64',
     'linux-s390x',
     'mac-amd64',
     'mac-arm64',
@@ -135,6 +136,8 @@ def arch_normalized(rosetta=False):
         if machine == 'arm64':
             return machine
         return 'armv6l'
+    if machine == 'riscv64':
+        return machine
     if machine.endswith('64'):
         return 'amd64'
     if machine.endswith('86'):
--
